{#
  One place, on a map.

  Progressive enhancement, like the network above it: the coordinates are
  already printed in the details list on this page, so nothing is lost when
  Leaflet does not load. The container stays empty and the status line says so.

  Every value the script needs arrives as a data attribute, escaped by
  autoescape. There is no inline script and no inline style, so the CSP needs
  no exception for this section.

  With no MAP_TILE_URL configured the marker draws on a plain canvas: correct
  relative position, no basemap, and no request to anybody but this server.
#}
{% if point %}
  <section class="map-section">
    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p class="hint">
      {% if point.precision == 'exact' %}
        Located exactly.
      {% elif point.precision == 'approximate' %}
        Located approximately — the point marks the settlement, not a building.
      {% elif point.precision == 'region' %}
        Located to a region only — the point marks an area, not a site.
      {% else %}
        Precision unrecorded; treat the position as indicative.
      {% endif %}
      {% if not mapTileUrl %}
        No basemap is configured, so only the marker is drawn.
      {% endif %}
    </p>

    <div
      id="place-map"
      class="map-canvas"
      data-latitude="{{ point.latitude }}"
      data-longitude="{{ point.longitude }}"
      data-title="{{ point.title }}"
      data-precision="{{ point.precision }}"
      data-tile-url="{{ mapTileUrl }}"
      data-tile-attribution="{{ mapTileAttribution }}"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Map showing the location of {{ point.title }}"
    ></div>

    <p id="place-map-status" class="muted small" role="status"></p>
  </section>
{% endif %}
